/P 61 0 R
/E (Traditional software development has been the standard approach for decades. It involves designing, coding, testing, deploying, and maintaining applications using programming languages and software engineering principles. Although this method provides complete flexibility and customization, it often requires large development teams, long project timelines, and significant financial investment. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (In contrast, low-code development has emerged as a modern software development methodology that simplifies application creation through graphical interfaces, reusable components, and workflow automation. It enables faster application development while reducing dependency on highly skilled programmers. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
